1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,000
Threatened by a ruthless demon, humanity was on the brink of destruction.

2
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:16,000
All seemed lost until a lone mage stepped forward and took up the fight.

3
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:28,000
After his triumph, he was hailed as the Wizard King, and his story became legend.

4
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:36,000
emos

5
00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:41,000
clue

6
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:43,000
guy

7
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:47,000
クオ

8
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:50,000
Flo

9
00:00:50,000 --> 00:01:19,980
Thank you.

10
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:49,980
Thank you.

11
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:52,000
Thank you.

12
00:02:21,000 --> 00:02:25,860
Some time after the two met, the Black Bulls were sent out on a dungeon-clearing mission.

13
00:02:26,100 --> 00:02:30,080
They battled a Diamond Kingdom mage named Mars, and Asta was gravely injured.

14
00:02:30,440 --> 00:02:34,220
Noelle had gone out to gather restorative herbs for her wounded squadmate.

15
00:02:34,220 --> 00:02:37,220
Come on, where is it?

16
00:02:38,620 --> 00:02:39,500
That's the one?

17
00:02:41,300 --> 00:02:42,180
Excuse me.

18
00:02:42,540 --> 00:02:43,880
You there with the silver hair?

19
00:02:44,160 --> 00:02:44,680
Yes, hello.

20
00:02:44,820 --> 00:02:45,480
Do you have a second?

21
00:02:47,080 --> 00:02:49,420
I'm sorry to bother you, but it won't take long.

22
00:02:49,420 --> 00:02:53,300
I just wanted a closer look at something of yours.

23
00:02:53,480 --> 00:02:55,500
Like I said, it'll only take a second.

24
00:02:55,900 --> 00:02:56,880
Why, you?

25
00:02:58,020 --> 00:02:58,500
What?

26
00:02:58,660 --> 00:02:59,460
You hurt!

27
00:03:01,860 --> 00:03:03,480
Wait, no, it's not like that!

28
00:03:03,600 --> 00:03:04,400
Please, I swear!

29
00:03:04,860 --> 00:03:06,740
Oh, yeah, then what is it like, huh?

30
00:03:06,740 --> 00:03:10,400
How's a man supposed to get a decent nap with all this screaming going on?

31
00:03:10,600 --> 00:03:11,440
Is that Noelle?

32
00:03:11,780 --> 00:03:12,780
Shut up!

33
00:03:15,960 --> 00:03:17,420
Don't let him touch me!

34
00:03:17,420 --> 00:03:23,040
You've got it all wrong, I'm not some kind of creep.

35
00:03:23,320 --> 00:03:24,720
I just want a real quick look.

36
00:03:25,000 --> 00:03:26,540
Please, I'm even willing to pay you.

37
00:03:26,620 --> 00:03:27,720
Just a peek, that's all.

38
00:03:29,640 --> 00:03:30,120
Oh.

39
00:03:37,440 --> 00:03:38,620
Feel my wrath!

40
00:03:38,740 --> 00:03:41,120
Pan is only one letter away from pain!

41
00:03:41,440 --> 00:03:43,400
Poor thing, it must have been so frightening

42
00:03:43,400 --> 00:03:45,820
being set upon by a vile man like that.

43
00:03:45,820 --> 00:03:47,920
What were you trying to do to her?

44
00:03:48,040 --> 00:03:50,160
She came running in, scared out of her mind.

45
00:03:50,360 --> 00:03:52,740
You're lucky we busted you up instead of killing you.

46
00:03:53,340 --> 00:03:55,040
Please, it's not how it looks.

47
00:03:55,200 --> 00:03:56,400
I was robbed, that's why.

48
00:03:56,420 --> 00:03:58,000
Nobody wants to hear it, freak.

49
00:03:58,340 --> 00:04:01,140
We should let him loose, then we can capture him again!

50
00:04:01,720 --> 00:04:04,240
You don't deserve to live in the same world as Marie.

51
00:04:05,160 --> 00:04:05,860
Now die.

52
00:04:05,940 --> 00:04:09,280
Yes, Knight's Headquarters, this is Finral reporting for the Black Bulls.

53
00:04:09,680 --> 00:04:13,140
We have a pervert in custody here, and we'll be bringing him in at once.

54
00:04:13,140 --> 00:04:14,240
No, please don't.

55
00:04:14,240 --> 00:04:15,960
I can explain, this is a misunderstanding.

56
00:04:16,960 --> 00:04:18,840
Misunderstanding works at the tavern, I think.

57
00:04:19,160 --> 00:04:21,620
I think we're having some communication issues.

58
00:04:21,700 --> 00:04:22,080
Zell?

59
00:04:22,580 --> 00:04:23,200
Hold on.

60
00:04:24,080 --> 00:04:24,420
Asta?

61
00:04:25,340 --> 00:04:27,500
Whoa, you're not looking so good, are you okay?

62
00:04:28,120 --> 00:04:28,820
Sort of.

63
00:04:29,140 --> 00:04:32,220
But enough about me, it seems you made it into a Magic Knight squad.

64
00:04:32,580 --> 00:04:33,020
Congratulations.

65
00:04:34,200 --> 00:04:34,440
Hmm.

66
00:04:34,440 --> 00:04:37,560
So it was all a misunderstanding?

67
00:04:38,160 --> 00:04:40,080
You were robbed and they took your clothes?

68
00:04:40,360 --> 00:04:41,980
You could have told us that earlier.

69
00:04:42,740 --> 00:04:45,380
I tried, but you weren't exactly in a listening mood.

70
00:04:45,620 --> 00:04:47,500
Yeah, details, details, who cares?

71
00:04:47,660 --> 00:04:48,400
Here you go.

72
00:04:48,740 --> 00:04:51,100
It's like I always say, better bread than dead.

73
00:04:51,420 --> 00:04:52,440
Oh, sure, thanks.

74
00:04:52,440 --> 00:04:54,680
We don't get new friends very often.

75
00:04:54,900 --> 00:04:56,940
I hope you'll tell me more about yourself.

76
00:04:56,940 --> 00:04:57,940
What's wrong?

77
00:04:58,460 --> 00:05:00,840
Zell, I gotta say, you look pretty familiar.

78
00:05:01,500 --> 00:05:03,000
Have we met somewhere before?

79
00:05:03,640 --> 00:05:04,300
Oh, no.

80
00:05:04,520 --> 00:05:06,300
I think I would remember meeting you.

81
00:05:06,440 --> 00:05:08,840
How'd you end up at her hideout anyway, old man?

82
00:05:09,300 --> 00:05:10,300
Oh, I forgot.

83
00:05:11,020 --> 00:05:12,980
Excuse me, but you're Noelle, aren't you?

84
00:05:13,280 --> 00:05:15,380
I'm really sorry for frightening you like that.

85
00:05:15,880 --> 00:05:18,120
I wanted to ask you about your wand, that's all.

86
00:05:19,100 --> 00:05:20,500
That's what you wanted to see?

87
00:05:20,980 --> 00:05:21,400
Yes.

88
00:05:22,120 --> 00:05:23,380
I think I know it's Maker.

89
00:05:23,960 --> 00:05:26,800
A woman named Domina I've been seeking for a while now.

90
00:05:27,360 --> 00:05:27,800
Domina?

91
00:05:28,240 --> 00:05:29,480
I remember that name.

92
00:05:29,580 --> 00:05:30,980
She's your fiancée, isn't she?

93
00:05:31,620 --> 00:05:32,240
All right.

94
00:05:33,140 --> 00:05:34,680
But I don't think she made this.

95
00:05:34,760 --> 00:05:36,560
The person who gave it to me was named Code.

96
00:05:36,700 --> 00:05:38,720
Doesn't sound like this Domina you're looking for.

97
00:05:39,200 --> 00:05:39,940
It is, though.

98
00:05:40,460 --> 00:05:41,020
It's her.

99
00:05:42,020 --> 00:05:44,660
You see, her full name is actually Dominante Code.

100
00:05:45,000 --> 00:05:45,860
Where did you get it?

101
00:05:45,860 --> 00:05:48,360
From a stall in the Castletown's Black Market.

102
00:05:49,400 --> 00:05:50,220
The Castletown.

103
00:05:50,780 --> 00:05:51,460
Thank you.

104
00:05:54,880 --> 00:05:55,860
Domina's alive!

105
00:05:55,960 --> 00:05:57,340
That's awesome news, Zell!

106
00:05:57,520 --> 00:05:58,580
Well, go get her!

107
00:05:58,900 --> 00:06:00,240
What are you waiting for?

108
00:06:00,420 --> 00:06:00,920
You're right.

109
00:06:01,660 --> 00:06:02,420
I should go.

110
00:06:02,680 --> 00:06:03,320
Right now.

111
00:06:03,580 --> 00:06:04,100
Thank you.

112
00:06:04,480 --> 00:06:05,500
I can take you there.

113
00:06:07,080 --> 00:06:08,320
Noelle, listen.

114
00:06:08,780 --> 00:06:12,220
Because of you, I'm going to be reunited with the woman I love.

115
00:06:12,700 --> 00:06:13,180
Finally.

116
00:06:14,120 --> 00:06:14,860
Thank you.

117
00:06:15,860 --> 00:06:17,480
I didn't do anything, though.

118
00:06:17,940 --> 00:06:19,700
Captain, sir, am I free to leave now?

119
00:06:20,480 --> 00:06:21,940
Yeah, sure, why not?

120
00:06:22,320 --> 00:06:25,160
But don't go blabbing about how we falsely imprisoned you.

121
00:06:25,380 --> 00:06:27,740
You're the one talking about false imprisonment.

122
00:06:27,940 --> 00:06:29,120
Shut it, portal boy.

123
00:06:29,680 --> 00:06:32,880
Well, speaking of which, use your spatial magic to send them on their way.

124
00:06:33,020 --> 00:06:33,880
Then we'll be square.

125
00:06:34,400 --> 00:06:35,720
I need a dump and a nap.

126
00:06:35,720 --> 00:06:39,800
I appreciate it.

127
00:06:40,140 --> 00:06:42,640
I should get going or it's going to be too hard to say goodbye.

128
00:06:44,100 --> 00:06:44,940
See ya, Asta.

129
00:06:45,400 --> 00:06:48,400
I'm glad our paths crossed again, even if it wasn't for long.

130
00:06:48,680 --> 00:06:50,980
Now, go out and become the Wizard King.

131
00:06:51,140 --> 00:06:51,860
Sure thing!

132
00:06:51,860 --> 00:06:53,900
And you go and live happily ever after.

133
00:07:00,620 --> 00:07:01,800
Everyone, get down!

134
00:07:02,500 --> 00:07:02,880
Huh?

135
00:07:03,860 --> 00:07:04,700
Oh, cool!

136
00:07:04,880 --> 00:07:06,020
Someone's attacking us!

137
00:07:06,280 --> 00:07:08,280
It's probably the people who were after me.

138
00:07:08,560 --> 00:07:11,000
So, sounds like it's time to get out of here.

139
00:07:11,160 --> 00:07:11,380
Uh-oh.

140
00:07:12,500 --> 00:07:13,860
What the hell is this?

141
00:07:14,080 --> 00:07:17,040
Whoever woke me up just turned themselves a-killin'.

142
00:07:17,040 --> 00:07:24,180
There's been no movement so far.

143
00:07:24,620 --> 00:07:26,900
Strange Master Fonzel didn't leave at once.

144
00:07:27,140 --> 00:07:28,800
That's what I would have expected him to do.

145
00:07:29,120 --> 00:07:30,860
For now, let's watch and wait.

146
00:07:31,340 --> 00:07:34,720
Squads one through four, maintain your formation and begin a steady advance.

147
00:07:35,240 --> 00:07:37,780
Squads five and six, continue to stand ready at the rear.

148
00:07:38,940 --> 00:07:39,700
That building.

149
00:07:40,360 --> 00:07:42,200
It looks like some sort of dormitory.

150
00:07:42,560 --> 00:07:42,960
Yes.

151
00:07:43,580 --> 00:07:46,180
I ought to be on my way now, Commander Galio.

152
00:07:46,600 --> 00:07:48,000
A portal, if you wouldn't mind.

153
00:07:48,420 --> 00:07:51,440
You want a little insurance in case our sneak attack fails.

154
00:07:52,040 --> 00:07:52,340
Huh.

155
00:07:53,000 --> 00:07:55,380
I honestly don't know what you're so worried about.

156
00:07:55,800 --> 00:07:59,300
We'd be a real laughingstock if we couldn't pull off an operation like this.

157
00:08:00,120 --> 00:08:01,780
I'm not sure I like your attitude.

158
00:08:02,480 --> 00:08:04,620
You remember who allowed you to live, right?

159
00:08:05,160 --> 00:08:07,460
I'm aware that I owe you my life, Commander.

160
00:08:07,460 --> 00:08:09,380
And don't forget it.

161
00:08:09,640 --> 00:08:12,720
Since I'm in your debt, I'll offer you a little advice.

162
00:08:13,960 --> 00:08:16,920
Defeating my old teacher won't be easy.

163
00:08:21,260 --> 00:08:22,800
Squad one, scout reporting.

164
00:08:23,080 --> 00:08:24,860
We're within 65 feet of the building.

165
00:08:24,860 --> 00:08:25,200
Good.

166
00:08:25,520 --> 00:08:26,280
Prepare to charge.

167
00:08:30,280 --> 00:08:31,720
The target's on the move.

168
00:08:31,900 --> 00:08:32,400
After him.

169
00:08:36,200 --> 00:08:37,960
Lightning creation magic!

170
00:08:38,520 --> 00:08:39,920
Thunderbolt destruction!

171
00:08:39,920 --> 00:08:42,540
Go flame magic!

172
00:08:42,540 --> 00:08:44,680
Prison, death, scattershot!

173
00:08:50,680 --> 00:08:51,620
Well, all right.

174
00:08:51,700 --> 00:08:52,700
I didn't see that coming.

175
00:08:53,080 --> 00:08:54,460
Our surprise attack worked.

176
00:08:54,600 --> 00:08:56,660
Guess these guys aren't so tough after all, huh?

177
00:08:56,660 --> 00:08:59,500
Yeah, too bad.

178
00:08:59,760 --> 00:09:03,720
But at least there are lots of them, so smashing their kneecaps ought to keep us entertained for a while.

179
00:09:07,000 --> 00:09:09,340
I want squads one and two to stay on the target.

180
00:09:09,580 --> 00:09:10,920
So you're in charge here?

181
00:09:14,300 --> 00:09:17,380
The sooner this is over with, the sooner I can visit Marie.

182
00:09:17,380 --> 00:09:19,960
See how you like my mirror magic.

183
00:09:20,100 --> 00:09:20,980
Reflect refrain.

184
00:09:24,120 --> 00:09:25,320
What's going on here?

185
00:09:32,740 --> 00:09:35,360
I got a nap to finish, so let's make this quick.

186
00:09:43,020 --> 00:09:44,140
Dark magic.

187
00:09:45,200 --> 00:09:46,200
Dark, look!

188
00:09:46,200 --> 00:09:48,620
Lightless Slash!

189
00:09:54,620 --> 00:09:56,340
I don't care who you are.

190
00:09:56,680 --> 00:09:59,100
Nobody ever lays a hand on my food!

191
00:10:03,280 --> 00:10:04,560
Hey, numbskulls.

192
00:10:04,720 --> 00:10:06,320
Save some of the fun for me.

193
00:10:07,020 --> 00:10:07,860
A water barrier.

194
00:10:08,640 --> 00:10:10,460
It's not meant to block attacks from out here,

195
00:10:10,560 --> 00:10:13,300
but to keep their own spells from destroying the place?

196
00:10:16,200 --> 00:10:18,320
You're the CO?

197
00:10:18,620 --> 00:10:23,860
Fonzo, then you, if you care about our hostage at all, you better get your traitor's hands off me.

198
00:10:23,980 --> 00:10:24,500
A hostage?

199
00:10:25,020 --> 00:10:25,340
Who?

200
00:10:25,840 --> 00:10:26,940
Don't me not take code.

201
00:10:27,380 --> 00:10:28,640
Mariella's on her way now.

202
00:10:28,640 --> 00:10:33,320
You may not have known where she had gone into hiding, but we did.

203
00:10:33,820 --> 00:10:34,760
Now let me go.

204
00:10:34,980 --> 00:10:35,620
Whoa-wee!

205
00:10:35,800 --> 00:10:37,380
Captain Yami is so amazing.

206
00:10:37,640 --> 00:10:40,000
Everything's playing out exactly like he said it would.

207
00:10:40,580 --> 00:10:41,020
What?

208
00:10:41,020 --> 00:10:45,460
My squad mates are going via portal to visit a lady by the name of Domina.

209
00:10:45,700 --> 00:10:48,440
I don't think your hostage will be a hostage for much longer.

210
00:10:49,120 --> 00:10:50,200
Who are you?

211
00:10:50,200 --> 00:10:59,120
How long were you going to wait to come and get me?

212
00:10:59,260 --> 00:11:03,220
A poor helpless woman hiding from a bunch of killers, and you just leave me here?

213
00:11:03,400 --> 00:11:05,840
You're lucky I'm still alive, you useless jerk!

214
00:11:05,840 --> 00:11:08,880
I was so worried.

215
00:11:09,500 --> 00:11:13,420
When you didn't come looking for me, I thought you might have gotten hurt.

216
00:11:14,140 --> 00:11:15,880
I'm a little more hurt now.

217
00:11:16,600 --> 00:11:17,960
Thank you for bringing him.

218
00:11:18,640 --> 00:11:21,840
I know I threw in a little extra, but I never thought you'd do this.

219
00:11:23,460 --> 00:11:26,300
I guess that means Bruce was right about you all along.

220
00:11:26,600 --> 00:11:27,480
I should have known.

221
00:11:28,040 --> 00:11:29,340
I'm not so sure.

222
00:11:29,340 --> 00:11:31,500
And this young man must be Asta.

223
00:11:31,840 --> 00:11:32,920
You know about me?

224
00:11:33,260 --> 00:11:36,440
I heard you were a tough-looking kid, and it seems like it's true.

225
00:11:36,640 --> 00:11:37,300
From who?

226
00:11:39,020 --> 00:11:39,340
Well...

227
00:11:42,060 --> 00:11:50,860
What are you doing here?

228
00:11:54,380 --> 00:11:54,900
Hmm?

229
00:11:56,220 --> 00:11:57,980
I don't plan to hurt anyone.

230
00:11:57,980 --> 00:12:01,320
Besides, how much damage can one girl possibly do on her own?

231
00:12:01,820 --> 00:12:04,340
You beat up your teacher and tried to kidnap him!

232
00:12:04,620 --> 00:12:05,880
Why should we trust you?

233
00:12:06,180 --> 00:12:08,040
My intentions are in no way malicious.

234
00:12:08,480 --> 00:12:09,920
I am simply using you.

235
00:12:10,260 --> 00:12:12,380
What do you mean?

236
00:12:12,720 --> 00:12:14,300
I recognize those robes.

237
00:12:14,400 --> 00:12:16,200
You're the Black Bulls squad, aren't you?

238
00:12:16,800 --> 00:12:19,600
Didn't Mariela know that when she ordered us to attack?

239
00:12:20,940 --> 00:12:24,660
Hold on, you're telling us you sent your own men to storm the Black Bulls' hideout,

240
00:12:24,760 --> 00:12:25,800
hoping they'd get crushed?

241
00:12:25,800 --> 00:12:30,640
Meanwhile, I came here to the Black Market and informed Domina that Master Fonzel would

242
00:12:30,640 --> 00:12:31,620
be arriving soon.

243
00:12:32,160 --> 00:12:33,960
I wanted to ensure she was prepared.

244
00:12:34,560 --> 00:12:36,980
However, I didn't expect you to get here so quickly.

245
00:12:38,020 --> 00:12:39,000
This is a map.

246
00:12:39,660 --> 00:12:42,140
I've researched escape routes and plotted them on it.

247
00:12:42,140 --> 00:12:44,840
I don't understand why you would do this, though.

248
00:12:45,320 --> 00:12:45,940
Nor I.

249
00:12:46,580 --> 00:12:48,680
To strike a blow against the Diamond Kingdom.

250
00:12:49,440 --> 00:12:51,640
A number of their assassins are now out of commission.

251
00:12:52,300 --> 00:12:54,540
Master Fonzel and Domina will be able to escape.

252
00:12:54,940 --> 00:12:59,000
So in other words, I set a plan in motion that would badly damage the organization.

253
00:13:00,080 --> 00:13:00,980
This is revenge.

254
00:13:01,580 --> 00:13:03,360
Mine against those who have controlled me.

255
00:13:03,880 --> 00:13:04,760
Why now?

256
00:13:04,760 --> 00:13:07,560
Much like my teacher, I'm tired.

257
00:13:08,020 --> 00:13:09,740
I can't do what they ask of me anymore.

258
00:13:13,100 --> 00:13:17,480
That said, I don't believe I have the strength to stay on the run for my whole life.

259
00:13:18,120 --> 00:13:20,020
It wasn't easy, but I made a decision.

260
00:13:20,860 --> 00:13:24,840
Exact my revenge and then turn myself into the Clover Kingdom's magic knights.

261
00:13:24,840 --> 00:13:26,880
You were going to turn yourself in?

262
00:13:27,800 --> 00:13:30,980
I was nearby, waiting for the circumstances to properly align.

263
00:13:31,820 --> 00:13:36,020
I watched as Master Fonzel approached the Black Bull's hideout and saw him dragged inside.

264
00:13:36,660 --> 00:13:39,900
I thought if I sent those troops against you, you would annihilate them for me.

265
00:13:40,600 --> 00:13:42,080
Thank you for consulting us.

266
00:13:42,220 --> 00:13:43,960
She makes it sound so easy.

267
00:13:44,560 --> 00:13:46,640
And now, will you please take me into custody?

268
00:13:47,120 --> 00:13:48,740
Then we all get what we want.

269
00:13:49,400 --> 00:13:50,800
Think about this, Nariela.

270
00:13:51,000 --> 00:13:51,920
Do you know what you're asking?

271
00:13:51,920 --> 00:13:55,040
You could be subjected to extreme punishment.

272
00:13:55,520 --> 00:13:57,820
The Clover Kingdom won't forget your past crimes.

273
00:13:58,260 --> 00:14:01,840
And the organization can still reach you, even if you're in somebody else's custody.

274
00:14:02,400 --> 00:14:04,000
I'm willing to accept that.

275
00:14:04,540 --> 00:14:06,520
Yes, as long as my life is spared.

276
00:14:08,600 --> 00:14:10,500
I've been thinking about what you said.

277
00:14:11,320 --> 00:14:14,240
We have to find our own hope, our own reason for living.

278
00:14:14,940 --> 00:14:15,240
Right?

279
00:14:15,680 --> 00:14:16,760
Yeah, what about it?

280
00:14:17,360 --> 00:14:19,020
It was obnoxious and overbearing.

281
00:14:19,020 --> 00:14:22,340
That said, it was also moving.

282
00:14:23,000 --> 00:14:24,040
And sort of dashing.

283
00:14:24,500 --> 00:14:25,740
Oh, you think so?

284
00:14:27,640 --> 00:14:32,940
Whatever punishment I might receive is the price I have to pay to atone for my crimes and begin a new life.

285
00:14:33,500 --> 00:14:36,640
So no matter how severe it is, I'll bear it without complaint.

286
00:14:37,880 --> 00:14:38,420
I see.

287
00:14:39,160 --> 00:14:40,660
I've had enough of this!

288
00:14:40,660 --> 00:14:47,100
Galio, sir, you're the Assassin Corps' commander and you've abandoned your troops.

289
00:14:47,280 --> 00:14:47,900
That's horrible.

290
00:14:48,380 --> 00:14:50,100
And what do you call what you did?

291
00:14:50,300 --> 00:14:53,720
If you want so desperately to be executed, I can oblige you.

292
00:14:54,080 --> 00:14:54,960
Everybody run.

293
00:14:55,540 --> 00:14:59,940
He may sound like a petty fool who's just full of hot air, but his magic's quite tricky.

294
00:15:00,640 --> 00:15:01,320
That's right!

295
00:15:01,460 --> 00:15:02,680
Spatial creation magic!

296
00:15:02,880 --> 00:15:03,940
Unopening red roof!

297
00:15:03,940 --> 00:15:12,620
Now, Spatial creation magic!

298
00:15:12,820 --> 00:15:13,660
Go, Riftmen!

299
00:15:17,660 --> 00:15:19,900
But what are these creepy red guys?

300
00:15:20,200 --> 00:15:21,460
And why's the room all red?

301
00:15:22,460 --> 00:15:24,440
Galio's initial spell created this place.

302
00:15:24,840 --> 00:15:27,640
And those figures are magic soldiers that can only exist here.

303
00:15:28,020 --> 00:15:29,500
They're not going to be easy to beat.

304
00:15:29,500 --> 00:15:32,460
But wait, hold on.

305
00:15:32,820 --> 00:15:35,240
You jumped in front of the spell without knowing what it did?

306
00:15:35,860 --> 00:15:39,060
If that had been offensive magic he was using, you could have died.

307
00:15:39,320 --> 00:15:40,000
Are you stupid?

308
00:15:40,700 --> 00:15:41,540
Well, maybe.

309
00:15:41,980 --> 00:15:43,320
So what if I am?

310
00:15:43,400 --> 00:15:46,540
I'd rather be stupid than just stand back and watch somebody die!

311
00:15:47,700 --> 00:15:51,340
And besides, something's changed since the last time we saw each other.

312
00:15:51,420 --> 00:15:53,200
I'm Asta of the Black Bulls now!

313
00:15:53,480 --> 00:15:55,040
But I'm still your enemy.

314
00:15:55,400 --> 00:15:56,360
I don't care!

315
00:15:56,640 --> 00:15:57,960
This is who I am!

316
00:15:57,960 --> 00:16:00,680
If someone needs help, I'll help them as much as I want!

317
00:16:01,240 --> 00:16:01,820
You got it?

318
00:16:04,300 --> 00:16:08,600
But hey, if you want to give me some backup while I'm at it, I won't mind!

319
00:16:09,700 --> 00:16:14,220
I may not be as altruistic as he is, but I can't stand by and watch a student suffer.

320
00:16:14,600 --> 00:16:17,380
So come on, let's work together and get through this!

321
00:16:17,820 --> 00:16:18,960
Get through this?

322
00:16:19,840 --> 00:16:20,820
How can we?

323
00:16:21,340 --> 00:16:21,780
Easy!

324
00:16:22,380 --> 00:16:23,820
This is nothing!

325
00:16:23,820 --> 00:16:28,400
No, impossible!

326
00:16:30,540 --> 00:16:34,120
Yeah, Knight's Headquarters, this is Yami of the Black Bulls.

327
00:16:34,740 --> 00:16:37,080
We got a bunch of troublemakers rounded up out here.

328
00:16:37,940 --> 00:16:39,040
Come and get him, would you?

329
00:16:39,040 --> 00:16:44,600
That's a lot of mages to have hunting you.

330
00:16:45,200 --> 00:16:48,780
Who is this Fonzel person and what did he do to get so many people sicked on him?

331
00:16:49,400 --> 00:16:50,300
Wait, hold on.

332
00:16:50,580 --> 00:16:51,720
Don't you mean Zell?

333
00:16:52,660 --> 00:16:55,380
No, according to Gray, his full name is actually Fonzel.

334
00:16:55,380 --> 00:17:01,340
Ah, that's right, he's Fonzel Kruger.

335
00:17:01,860 --> 00:17:04,860
He was the commander of the Diamond Kingdom's invading army.

336
00:17:05,300 --> 00:17:08,100
I met the guy on the battlefield a really long time ago.

337
00:17:09,060 --> 00:17:09,500
Seriously?

338
00:17:10,180 --> 00:17:14,300
I heard he moved from commanding the army to training their soldiers, but I guess he must

339
00:17:14,300 --> 00:17:18,220
have deserted, which would explain why everybody and their mom was trying to get to him.

340
00:17:18,220 --> 00:17:21,360
I realize it isn't my place to ask this, sir.

341
00:17:22,100 --> 00:17:26,180
And correct me if I'm wrong, but did we just help a high-ranking member of our greatest

342
00:17:26,180 --> 00:17:27,640
enemy's military escape?

343
00:17:28,260 --> 00:17:29,320
Sounds about right.

344
00:17:30,760 --> 00:17:31,280
McGauch?

345
00:17:31,880 --> 00:17:32,740
Yes, Captain?

346
00:17:33,080 --> 00:17:34,720
Never speak of this again.

347
00:17:35,480 --> 00:17:36,620
My lips are sealed.

348
00:17:37,000 --> 00:17:38,680
Please give me a week of Marie leave.

349
00:17:39,100 --> 00:17:41,680
You're only supposed to see her once a month, aren't you?

350
00:17:41,680 --> 00:17:46,360
I'll watch her so surreptitiously for all 168 hours that nobody will know.

351
00:17:46,360 --> 00:17:48,660
Man, you've got some serious issues.

352
00:17:49,940 --> 00:17:54,660
And so, the case of the creepy naked man and the mysterious attack on the Black Bull's

353
00:17:54,660 --> 00:17:56,640
hideout was put to rest at last.

354
00:18:02,380 --> 00:18:05,060
Are you sure it's okay for us to leave like this?

355
00:18:05,360 --> 00:18:09,240
I'm worried that it'll only cause all of you more trouble in the long run if we just

356
00:18:09,240 --> 00:18:10,120
up and vanish.

357
00:18:10,380 --> 00:18:14,220
Captain Yami didn't have any problems with you guys going, so I'm sure it's fine.

358
00:18:14,700 --> 00:18:15,540
Don't you think so?

359
00:18:16,360 --> 00:18:17,640
Yes, sure.

360
00:18:18,160 --> 00:18:22,040
Not fine, and it'll probably turn into something extremely not fine.

361
00:18:22,200 --> 00:18:23,960
Are you sure you're okay with this, though?

362
00:18:24,460 --> 00:18:26,480
Mariella isn't exactly the nicest person.

363
00:18:26,840 --> 00:18:29,140
All the terrible things I did were under duress.

364
00:18:29,620 --> 00:18:33,040
Galeo and his assassin corps were going to kidnap me and hold me hostage.

365
00:18:33,440 --> 00:18:35,320
She's the one who put a stop to that, remember?

366
00:18:36,140 --> 00:18:40,160
Besides, if you think about it, Mariella here is the reason my cell and I were reunited.

367
00:18:40,160 --> 00:18:45,220
Honestly, there's such a thing as being too nice, you know?

368
00:18:45,220 --> 00:18:48,420
You're one to talk, you and your pushover squad.

369
00:18:48,900 --> 00:18:51,940
Honestly, I manipulated all of you so easily, it was ridiculous.

370
00:18:52,740 --> 00:18:55,140
I never asked for your help, and I don't need it.

371
00:18:55,280 --> 00:18:57,520
I can get by just fine without anybody else.

372
00:18:57,620 --> 00:18:59,660
The only person you need in your life is you.

373
00:18:59,820 --> 00:19:01,860
You've been telling yourself that for a while, huh?

374
00:19:01,860 --> 00:19:06,660
Taking on the burden alone is actually surprisingly easy, isn't it?

375
00:19:06,760 --> 00:19:10,240
You just keep saying to yourself as long as you can get through it, you'll be fine.

376
00:19:10,420 --> 00:19:12,580
There's no need to consider the people around you.

377
00:19:12,760 --> 00:19:14,960
So there's not really much thinking involved at all.

378
00:19:16,040 --> 00:19:18,980
I hate to tell you, but that's off the table now.

379
00:19:19,240 --> 00:19:21,980
Because once you have people in your life who care about you,

380
00:19:22,100 --> 00:19:25,000
your problems and your decisions aren't only your own anymore.

381
00:19:28,280 --> 00:19:29,040
That's right.

382
00:19:29,040 --> 00:19:31,140
Now you've got to think about them, too.

383
00:19:31,480 --> 00:19:33,000
So you better get used to it.

384
00:19:35,200 --> 00:19:38,060
I guess I'm not the only one here with personality issues.

385
00:19:38,360 --> 00:19:41,020
Well, it's not like I care what you think anyway.

386
00:19:42,460 --> 00:19:45,320
All right, we should get going or it's going to be too hard.

387
00:19:46,280 --> 00:19:48,120
Hey, there's nothing to cry about.

388
00:19:48,300 --> 00:19:51,620
Remember, old man, you and me are guys who like to get things done.

389
00:19:51,680 --> 00:19:54,660
And like you said, there's no time for sitting around, so get to work.

390
00:19:54,980 --> 00:19:57,680
Go out there and make Domina as happy as you can.

391
00:19:57,680 --> 00:19:59,440
You're right.

392
00:19:59,700 --> 00:20:03,300
I was given more time when I thought I had none left, and I won't waste it.

393
00:20:03,740 --> 00:20:07,620
Together, Mariela, Domina, and I are going to live life to the fullest.

394
00:20:08,180 --> 00:20:09,120
That's the spirit!

395
00:20:11,640 --> 00:20:13,760
All right, once things settle down a bit.

396
00:20:13,840 --> 00:20:14,140
Great!

397
00:20:14,520 --> 00:20:15,540
Take care of yourself!

398
00:20:15,540 --> 00:20:22,780
Uh, and, well, I hate to ask this, but, uh, remember how you all thought I was a creep,

399
00:20:23,020 --> 00:20:25,980
but then I told you I was actually robbed and my clothes were taken?

400
00:20:29,100 --> 00:20:30,360
You're kidding, right?

401
00:20:30,640 --> 00:20:33,060
Do you think I could borrow some money?

402
00:20:34,420 --> 00:20:37,540
We should have just let the Diamond Kingdom have you!

403
00:20:37,540 --> 00:20:43,040
And that's the story of how Fonzel, Domina, and Mariela met the Black Bulls.

404
00:20:45,040 --> 00:20:48,260
Back in the present, Noel and Finral have called on Fonzel,

405
00:20:48,600 --> 00:20:51,760
hoping he might be able to help them find a way to heal Asta's arms.

406
00:20:52,220 --> 00:20:54,220
Domina, Mariela, how have you...

407
00:20:54,220 --> 00:20:55,620
Enough with the naked thing!

408
00:20:55,680 --> 00:20:56,440
You're a grown man!

409
00:20:56,520 --> 00:20:57,520
Keep your clothes on!

410
00:20:57,740 --> 00:20:57,980
Ow!

411
00:20:58,700 --> 00:20:59,100
Stop!

412
00:20:59,280 --> 00:21:00,120
It's not my fault!

413
00:21:00,200 --> 00:21:00,820
These things are supposed to happen to me!

414
00:21:00,820 --> 00:21:02,520
The house has already run down enough.

415
00:21:02,520 --> 00:21:04,440
Don't contribute to its sorry state.

416
00:21:07,120 --> 00:21:08,000
Oh, wow.

417
00:21:08,160 --> 00:21:08,860
Poor Asta.

418
00:21:08,980 --> 00:21:09,600
That's terrible.

419
00:21:09,820 --> 00:21:12,620
He's had quite an eventful life for someone who's still so young.

420
00:21:13,460 --> 00:21:16,100
His bad luck is inversely proportional to his height.

421
00:21:16,620 --> 00:21:17,820
Do you have any ideas?

422
00:21:18,200 --> 00:21:20,040
We have to find a way to heal him.

423
00:21:20,460 --> 00:21:21,660
Anything will be helpful.

424
00:21:22,220 --> 00:21:24,660
So, ancient hex magic, huh?

425
00:21:25,420 --> 00:21:26,760
Well, there is one place.

426
00:21:27,600 --> 00:21:29,880
My homeland, the Forest of Witches.

427
00:21:30,200 --> 00:21:31,600
You think they'd help?

428
00:21:31,600 --> 00:21:34,200
The Queen of the Witches' magic would.

429
00:21:45,140 --> 00:21:45,640
Hey!

430
00:21:46,220 --> 00:21:49,900
The smartest witch ever to grace the land of witches has come back to say hello!

431
00:21:50,440 --> 00:21:52,680
I have business here, so open up!

432
00:21:52,680 --> 00:21:53,520
Okay.

433
00:21:53,520 --> 00:22:08,720
THE KINDBAT

434
00:22:23,520 --> 00:22:53,500
Thank you.

435
00:22:53,520 --> 00:23:23,500
Thank you.

436
00:23:23,520 --> 00:23:25,520
Thank you.

